    96	## 2. F2: accepted signature encodings and rule-O policy
    97	
    98	**Rule O encoding (gpg slot; fallback kms slot).** Accepted: exactly one legacy-format signature packet, `0x88 u8`
    99	(body ≤ 255) or `0x89 u16` (256..1021), with a v4 body of type 0x00, algorithm 19, hash 8, shortest-form subpackets,
   100	two prefix octets, then MPIs r and s of 1..256 bits each with exact bit counts; r, s ∈ [1, n−1].
   101	
   102	- **Both low-S and high-S are accepted.** O-01 is low-S (s ≤ n/2). O-02 is its high-S twin (r, n−s). A test asserts
   103	  which is which (`test_O01_is_low_s_and_O02_is_its_high_s_twin`).
   104	- **DER is never an accepted input form.** The verifier builds the DER itself from the parsed MPIs. The analogue of
   105	  non-canonical DER, a non-minimal MPI, is `SIG_FORMAT` (O-15).
   106	
   107	| Rejected | Code | Vectors |
   108	|---|---|---|
   109	| OpenPGP-format header, non-shortest header, bare DER, raw r‖s, armor | `SIG_PACKET` | O-04..O-08 |
   110	| trailing / truncated | `TRAILING` / `TRUNCATED` | O-09, O-10 |
   111	| v5, type 0x01, algorithm 22, hash 10, MPI with leading zero, 257-bit MPI, r = 0 | `SIG_FORMAT` | O-11..O-17 |
   112	| r = n, s = n, r = 2²⁵⁶−1 | `SIG_POLICY` | O-18..O-20 |
   113	| prefix octets wrong, other document, other key | `SIG_INVALID` | O-21..O-23 |
   114	| rule-O packet in the hybrid kms slot | `SIG_FORMAT` | O-25 |
   115	
   116	**Rule-O signature policy** (V1-PROFILE §8, "Rule-O signature policy" and "Advisory metadata, structural
   117	validation"; `codec.sig_policy`). Every P vector is a correctly signed packet over its own hashed area.
   118	`TestRuleOPolicy::test_policy_vector_is_correctly_signed` checks that each one verifies when `sig_policy` is
   119	skipped, so each `SIG_POLICY` outcome is the policy's doing.
   120	
   121	- **Hashed area:**
   122	  - exactly one creation-time subpacket (type 2) with exactly 4 data octets, critical or not;
   123	  - no signature-expiration subpacket (type 3), critical or not;
   124	  - types 16 and 33 accepted, critical or not, with exact structure: at most one 16, of 8 octets; at most one 33, of
   125	    21 octets with first octet 04; if both are present, 16 equals the last 8 octets of 33;
   126	  - any other type is ignored if noncritical and a failure if critical.
   127	- **Unhashed area:** ignored entirely, critical bits included, after ENC's subpacket framing.
   128	
   129	| Case | Outcome | Vectors |
   130	|---|---|---|
   131	| creation time critical; GnuPG shape (hashed 2 + 33, unhashed 16); hashed 16 + 33 consistent; 16 + 33 both critical; unknown noncritical hashed type | `ACCEPT` | P-01..P-05 |
   132	| unhashed area holding a critical unknown, a critical expiration, malformed and inconsistent 16/33, and duplicate creation times | `ACCEPT` (ignored) | P-06 |
   133	| creation time missing, duplicated, 3, 5 or 0 data octets | `SIG_POLICY` | P-10..P-14 |
   134	| expiration, noncritical or critical | `SIG_POLICY` | P-15, P-16 |
   135	| unknown critical type; RFC-known type 4 marked critical | `SIG_POLICY` | P-17, P-18 |
   136	| type 16 of 7 octets; two type 16; type 33 of 20 octets; type 33 version 05; two type 33; 16/33 inconsistent; zero-data critical 33 | `SIG_POLICY` | P-19..P-25 |
   137	
   138	**Rule R (hybrid kms slot).** Accepted: exactly 3309 bytes that pass the FIPS 204 HintBitUnpack and z-bound
   139	conditions and verify under pure ML-DSA-65 with the empty context. Positive controls: a library `sign(F, context=b'')`
   140	signature (R-01) and an `EXTERNAL_MU`-style `sign_mu` signature (R-02, the issuer's path).
   141	
   142	| Rejected | Code | Vectors |
   143	|---|---|---|
   144	| length 0 | `SIG_EMPTY` | R-03 |
   145	| length 3308, ML-DSA-44 (2420) | `SIG_FORMAT` | R-04, R-06 |
   146	| length 3310, ML-DSA-87 (4627) | `LENGTH_CAP` | R-05, R-07 |
   147	| hint: nonzero padding, duplicate index, swapped indices (each decodes to the **same** h under a lax decoder), count ω+1, decreasing counts | `SIG_INVALID` | R-08..R-12 |
