   155	## 3. F3: public-key validation behaviour
   156	
   157	**P-256 (gpg packet; fallback kms SPKI; repository key).** The verifier requires:
   158	
   159	- the exact encoding: the 82-byte v4 packet body with prefix `13 08 2a8648ce3d030107 0203`, or the 26-byte SPKI prefix
   160	  plus 65 bytes;
   161	- an **uncompressed** point `04‖X‖Y`.
   162	
   163	It then checks **X < p, Y < p and the curve equation itself, before the EC constructor is called**. All of the
   164	following are `KEY_FORMAT`:
   165	
   166	| Case | Vectors |
   167	|---|---|
   168	| compressed point | K-05, K-17 |
   169	| hybrid 06/07 encoding | K-06 |
   170	| off-curve point | K-03, K-15 |
   171	| non-canonical X = x+p | K-04, K-16 |
   172	| non-canonical Y = y+p | K-36, K-37 |
   173	| other curves | K-09, K-18, K-19 |
   174	| wrong version, algorithm, MPI count or length | K-07, K-08, K-10..K-12 |
   175	| cross-slot encodings | K-13, K-20, K-21 |
   176	
   177	A bad repository key refuses the trust configuration (`TRUST_CONFIG_UNAUTHENTICATED`, B07).
   178	
   179	**Ordering, tested (P3R-02).** `TestPointBeforeConstructor` replaces `codec.ec`, for the codec module only, with a
   180	permissive stand-in whose constructor accepts anything:
   181	
   182	- **Rejected without the constructor ever being called:** X ≥ p (K-04, K-16), Y ≥ p (K-36, K-37), curve membership
   183	  (K-03, K-15, L-03, L-01), and representation (compressed, hybrid, leading 00 or 05).
   184	- **Positive controls reach the constructor with the exact (x, y):** K-01, K-02, K-35, K-14.
   185	
   186	So the verifier's own checks decide these cases, not the library's defaults. This matters because the library alone
   187	**accepts X ≥ p and Y ≥ p and reduces them** (LIB02, LIB09). Its DER loader also **accepts compressed-point SPKIs and
   188	other curves** (LIB03). The library does reject off-curve points by itself (LIB01), so for curve membership the
   189	verifier's check is shown, by the mock, to come first, but is redundant with this build.
   190	
   191	**ML-DSA-65 (hybrid kms).** The only check is the exact 1974-byte SPKI: OID 2.16.840.1.101.3.4.3.18, parameters
   192	absent, zero unused bits, minimal DER (K-22 accepted; K-24..K-34 `KEY_FORMAT`). There is no further public-key
   193	validation. Every 1952-byte string is a well-formed FIPS 204 key: the all-zero key is accepted (K-23), and the
   194	library accepts it too (LIB06). That is decoding behaviour, not a security claim about such a key. The library's
   195	generic DER loader would accept ML-DSA-44/-87 SPKIs as keys of their own parameter sets (LIB04); the verifier's
   196	exact-prefix rule rejects them (K-28, K-29).
