     4	   [pipeline.py:134](/home/tony/projects/tessera/service/issuer/tessera_issue/pipeline.py:134) saves the signature and marks its job satisfied before `siglog_add()` at line 141. If that log write fails, later polls can seal and ship using the saved signature while response delivery is delayed or missed. Fault injection produced **COMPLETE with only three signature-log entries**. The fourth hash remained in request metadata, but was absent from the append-only log. SQS short polling permits false-empty responses. [AWS documentation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-short-and-long-polling.html)  
     5	   **Fix:** durably log each response before making its signature eligible, and require that log record when sealing.
