    77	### Comments and clarified scope
    78	
    79	These are summaries of the author's comments and the clarifications discussed
    80	with the reviewer, not verbatim author quotations or additional model results.
    81	
    82	- **R6 — operational boundary.** The named operational environments are
    83	  illustrative, not exhaustive. GCP already participates in signing; another
    84	  provider's name does not establish independence. The requirement is
    85	  independence from the operational environment, assessed by actual roles,
    86	  credentials and release authorization. The author's concerns about trusting
    87	  third-party security services remain relevant. Tupay's developing key
    88	  mechanism is not a current Tessera requirement or dependency.
    89	- **R10 — prose linkage.** Acceptance is of P4's bounded classification result.
    90	  The prose correspondence to ProVerif acceptance is not a machine-checked
    91	  composition. Separate passing models can disagree about required checks,
    92	  their inputs or their outcomes; this is an assurance gap, not a demonstrated
    93	  exploit or evidence of end-to-end correctness. The author raised concern
    94	  about this boundary; acceptance does not close it.
    95	- **R13 — two abstract channels.** The author asked whether the list was
    96	  definitive. The clarified scope is exactly two modelled authority channels,
    97	  corresponding to DNS and the repository, under the stated compromise cases.
    98	  Concrete DNSSEC/git verification is outside the model. This is not a
    99	  general result for arbitrary channels or providers; signing infrastructure
