    35	| AJ6 verification materials | Owner: acquisition instructions that identify a compatible signed release and a trust configuration covering the receipt's evidence, authenticated under profile §15.9. Supported environment: one stated platform per release (V1: Linux x86-64). **AUTHOR** (recommendation): releases stay downloadable for as long as AJ2's publication runs, with 12 months' notice before support ends. | Owner and Author |
    36	| AJ7 capture notice | **AUTHOR.** Recommendation: promise to announce any known capture of the authority records or keys, within 7 days, through the channels that carry the release-key fingerprint. Detection is still not promised. | Author |
    37	
    38	## Limits
    39	
    40	| Item | Resolution | By |
    41	|---|---|---|
    42	| L1 window dates and closure | Both window endpoints are fixed and published before issuance preparation, at most 90 days apart. The actual dates stay OPEN until the dated operating record; a late first issuance does not extend the window. Signing stops 96 hours before the window ends (the runbook's operating margin, not a registered rule). Acceptance stops 120 hours before the end, so that every accepted request can complete or fail (S4) before signing stops. Only receipts that pass the registered window checks are shipped. Completed results stay retrievable for 30 days (S5). Closure is announced 14 days ahead on the service page. | Owner |
